1
00:00:01,335 --> 00:00:03,420
Thank you guys
for having us over.

2
00:00:03,462 --> 00:00:06,047
Yeah, this is fun.
Couples night.

3
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,549
Yeah, I don't know why
we don't hang out

4
00:00:07,591 --> 00:00:08,717
with married couples
more often.

5
00:00:08,759 --> 00:00:10,344
Well, because every time we do,

6
00:00:10,385 --> 00:00:14,055
you make jokes about swinging
and scare them away.

7
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:16,767
You mean
that Portuguese couple?

8
00:00:16,809 --> 00:00:19,060
Yeah, like you wouldn't
have done it.

9
00:00:20,604 --> 00:00:23,774
Hey, you guys,
I have great news.

10
00:00:23,816 --> 00:00:25,776
Ross, we're kind of
in the middle of dinner here.

11
00:00:25,818 --> 00:00:28,988
Oh, well, uh, I already ate,
but sure.

12
00:00:31,198 --> 00:00:32,533
Guess what happened
at work today.

13
00:00:32,574 --> 00:00:35,327
A dinosaur died
a million years ago?

14
00:00:35,369 --> 00:00:37,621
Uh, try 65 million
years ago,

15
00:00:37,663 --> 00:00:39,498
and then try shh!

16
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:43,293
My, uh, tenure review board
met today,

17
00:00:43,335 --> 00:00:45,295
and I hear it's looking
really good.

18
00:00:45,337 --> 00:00:46,421
Wow.
That's great.

19
00:00:46,463 --> 00:00:47,798
Do you have any idea

20
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:49,717
what this means
in academic circles, huh?

21
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:52,051
I am going to get laid.

22
00:00:54,013 --> 00:00:55,556
Hi, you guys.

23
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:57,725
Hey.
Ooh, Italian.

24
00:00:57,766 --> 00:01:00,477
Uh, no one... no one
wanted seconds, right?

25
00:01:00,519 --> 00:01:01,979
No, I'm-I'm good.

26
00:01:02,021 --> 00:01:03,522
Hey, you guys,

27
00:01:03,564 --> 00:01:04,899
you're never going
to believe it.

28
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:06,274
This headhunter called me.

29
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:07,735
I have a meeting tomorrow
with Gucci.

30
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:09,862
Gucci wants me.

31
00:01:09,904 --> 00:01:11,071
I'm up for tenure.

32
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:12,447
Congratulations.

33
00:01:12,489 --> 00:01:14,950
You too. What
are the odds?
Oh...

34
00:01:14,992 --> 00:01:15,951
Guess what?!

35
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:20,831
I finally got that seed
out of my teeth!

36
00:01:21,874 --> 00:01:24,292
I don't know
who I'm happiest for.

37
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:26,837
I do. He's been working
on that all day!

38
00:01:34,386 --> 00:01:38,891
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

39
00:01:38,933 --> 00:01:41,100
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

40
00:01:41,142 --> 00:01:44,730
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

41
00:01:44,772 --> 00:01:48,817
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

42
00:01:48,859 --> 00:01:50,986
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

43
00:01:51,028 --> 00:01:53,280
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

44
00:01:53,321 --> 00:01:57,158
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

45
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,703
♪ When the rain starts to pour ♪

46
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:02,247
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

47
00:02:02,289 --> 00:02:04,917
♪ Like I've been there before ♪

48
00:02:04,959 --> 00:02:07,669
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

49
00:02:07,711 --> 00:02:13,425
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

50
00:02:19,765 --> 00:02:23,310
Hey, Mon, was it weird changing
your name to Geller-Bing?

51
00:02:23,351 --> 00:02:27,230
No. No, it felt nice
to acknowledge this.

52
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:28,523
Where did you go to do it?

53
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:34,071
Um, the, uh...
the-the Ministry of Names...

54
00:02:34,113 --> 00:02:35,906
Bureau.

55
00:02:35,948 --> 00:02:38,117
You never did it!

56
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:44,832
I'm sorry. It's just the idea
of-of being an official Bing...

57
00:02:44,873 --> 00:02:47,584
Hey, I will have
you know that...

58
00:02:47,626 --> 00:02:49,753
Aw, who am I kidding?
Let's call the kid Geller

59
00:02:49,795 --> 00:02:51,922
and let Bing die with me.

60
00:02:53,715 --> 00:02:55,174
Here you go.
Thanks.

61
00:02:55,216 --> 00:02:56,927
Honey, would you want
me to take your name?

62
00:02:56,969 --> 00:02:58,679
Oh, it's up to you.

63
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:00,514
It's your name.
You've got to live with it.

64
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:03,017
All right, let's see.
Call me "Mrs. Hannigan."

65
00:03:03,058 --> 00:03:03,976
Mrs. Hannigan?

66
00:03:04,018 --> 00:03:04,977
What?! Can't you see

67
00:03:05,019 --> 00:03:06,478
I'm in the middle of something?!

68
00:03:08,105 --> 00:03:09,188
Ooh, I like it.

69
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:11,984
Hey, guys.
Hey, Joe.

70
00:03:12,026 --> 00:03:13,694
We got a couple things
we got to check out

71
00:03:13,735 --> 00:03:14,736
at the new house.

72
00:03:14,778 --> 00:03:15,821
You want to come
with us?

73
00:03:15,863 --> 00:03:18,115
No, thank you.

74
00:03:18,157 --> 00:03:19,741
Joey, I know you're not happy
about us moving,

75
00:03:19,783 --> 00:03:21,535
but you're the only one
who hasn't seen the house.

76
00:03:21,576 --> 00:03:23,662
Yeah, come with us.
You'll see how close
it is to the city.

77
00:03:23,704 --> 00:03:25,204
But, no, it's not close.

78
00:03:25,246 --> 00:03:26,707
You said it was in Escrow.

79
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:29,043
I couldn't even find that
on the map.

80
00:03:32,087 --> 00:03:34,089
Joey, please come.

81
00:03:34,131 --> 00:03:36,133
It would mean so much to us.

82
00:03:36,175 --> 00:03:38,844
You know what?

83
00:03:38,886 --> 00:03:40,179
You are my friends.

84
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,262
I want to be supportive.

85
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:42,723
I will come with you. Shotgun.

86
00:03:42,764 --> 00:03:43,932
Damn it!

87
00:03:43,974 --> 00:03:45,142
All right,
see you guys later.

88
00:03:45,184 --> 00:03:46,476
Okay.
We'll pick you up
at 11:00.

89
00:03:46,518 --> 00:03:49,521
I'm so glad
you're coming.

90
00:03:49,563 --> 00:03:52,399
Good for you. That
was really mature.

91
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:53,984
No. The only reason I'm going

92
00:03:54,026 --> 00:03:55,819
to their stupid new house
is so I can point out

93
00:03:55,861 --> 00:03:58,030
everything that's wrong with it
so they don't move.

94
00:03:58,072 --> 00:03:59,614
I'm going to make 'em stay here!

95
00:03:59,656 --> 00:04:02,450
You're a strange kind
of grownup.

96
00:04:05,037 --> 00:04:07,706
Joey, you can't make
someone do something
they don't want to do.

97
00:04:07,748 --> 00:04:09,416
Believe me,
there's something
I've been trying

98
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:10,918
to get Mike to do in
bed, and there's...

99
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:12,586
Whoa, whoa, whoa, hey, hey.

100
00:04:12,627 --> 00:04:14,755
Could we not talk
about that now?

101
00:04:14,796 --> 00:04:16,590
All right, prude.

102
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:21,762
Look, Monica and
Chandler really
love this house.

103
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:24,347
You are not going
to talk them into
staying here.

104
00:04:24,389 --> 00:04:26,349
Hey, hey, I can
convince people
to do anything.

105
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:28,852
You know, I bet you
I could even get Mike
to do that thing.

106
00:04:28,894 --> 00:04:30,896
What is it?

107
00:04:33,148 --> 00:04:35,943
I am not going to help you
do that!

108
00:04:35,984 --> 00:04:38,737
Oh, my... God!

109
00:04:44,451 --> 00:04:48,580
Hi, um, I'm here to see
Mr. Campbell with Gucci.

110
00:04:48,622 --> 00:04:51,708
The reservation's
probably under Gucci.

111
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:54,962
It's-it's spelled like "Gucky,"
which can be confusing.

112
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:57,089
Mr. Campbell's not here yet.

113
00:04:57,131 --> 00:04:59,633
Let me show you
to his table.

114
00:05:03,262 --> 00:05:05,055
Oh, my God,
that's my boss!

115
00:05:05,097 --> 00:05:06,556
You have to seat us
somewhere else.

116
00:05:06,598 --> 00:05:08,934
I'm sorry, that's always
Mr. Campbell's table.

117
00:05:08,976 --> 00:05:10,769
No, but my... but my boss
cannot see me.

118
00:05:10,811 --> 00:05:13,147
I'm interviewing
for another job.

119
00:05:13,188 --> 00:05:15,440
I know... with "Gucky."

120
00:05:15,482 --> 00:05:16,817
Shh!

121
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:18,944
Rachel?

122
00:05:18,986 --> 00:05:21,905
Hi, I'm on a date!

123
00:05:21,947 --> 00:05:24,449
That's... great.

124
00:05:24,491 --> 00:05:25,909
Yeah, it is, yeah.

125
00:05:25,951 --> 00:05:28,120
You know, it's tough.
Single mom, career.

126
00:05:28,162 --> 00:05:30,998
You got to get out there!

127
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:33,625
Well... you've got
a good energy.

128
00:05:33,667 --> 00:05:34,793
Oh...

129
00:05:34,835 --> 00:05:36,128
Rachel?
Yes, hi.

130
00:05:36,170 --> 00:05:37,129
James Campbell.

131
00:05:37,171 --> 00:05:38,130
Hi.
Hi.

132
00:05:38,172 --> 00:05:39,631
Excuse us.
Please.

133
00:05:39,673 --> 00:05:42,259
Okay. Oh...

134
00:05:42,301 --> 00:05:45,720
Well, now, he's cute.

135
00:05:45,762 --> 00:05:49,808
So... your resume
is quite impressive.

136
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:53,770
My... my resume?

137
00:05:53,812 --> 00:05:55,605
I wouldn't... I wouldn't call

138
00:05:55,647 --> 00:05:59,609
my-my online dating profile
a resume.

139
00:05:59,651 --> 00:06:01,611
Dating profile?
No, no, I'm...

140
00:06:01,653 --> 00:06:03,155
I'm talking about
the work resume...

141
00:06:03,197 --> 00:06:06,783
♪ La, la, la, la, la,
la, la, la, la... ♪

142
00:06:06,825 --> 00:06:11,663
Whatever happened to just
singing for no reason?

143
00:06:11,705 --> 00:06:14,541
Maybe people found it weird.

144
00:06:16,168 --> 00:06:18,128
So...

145
00:06:18,170 --> 00:06:20,339
why do you want to leave
Ralph Lauren?

146
00:06:20,379 --> 00:06:22,799
What?! I-I-I don't.

147
00:06:22,841 --> 00:06:25,510
You don't?
No, I-I love...
I love it there!

148
00:06:25,552 --> 00:06:27,595
If you don't want to leave,
why are we having this lunch?

149
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:31,308
( whispering ):
That is my boss.

150
00:06:31,350 --> 00:06:32,559
What?

151
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,686
That is my boss.

152
00:06:34,728 --> 00:06:36,604
That's Hugo Boss?
No...

153
00:06:43,402 --> 00:06:45,697
God, this place
is so depressing.

154
00:06:45,739 --> 00:06:48,158
If I had to work here,
I'd kill myself.

155
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:53,705
But you obviously haven't.

156
00:06:54,748 --> 00:06:56,583
How can I help you?

157
00:06:56,624 --> 00:06:58,335
Um, I need to change
my name, please.

158
00:06:58,377 --> 00:07:01,796
See, I need to change it, 'cause
I'm-I'm hiding from the law.

159
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:05,842
You're fun.

160
00:07:05,884 --> 00:07:08,427
You need to fill
out this form.

161
00:07:08,469 --> 00:07:11,098
Okay, well, just so I know-- I
don't know how it works exactly.

162
00:07:11,139 --> 00:07:13,808
See, my name is, um, Buffay, and
my husband's name is Hannigan,

163
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:16,770
so is it supposed to be
Buffay-Hannigan or
Hannigan-Buffay?

164
00:07:16,811 --> 00:07:18,521
It can be
anything you want.

165
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:20,523
Well, not anything.

166
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:22,276
Yeah. Anything.

167
00:07:22,317 --> 00:07:26,363
Oh, this could take a while.

168
00:07:27,406 --> 00:07:28,365
Get out of my line.
Okay.

169
00:07:34,288 --> 00:07:35,872
Hey.
Hey, Pheebs.

170
00:07:35,914 --> 00:07:38,666
Ooh, not anymore.
I changed it today.

171
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:40,752
Oh, I'm sorry,
"Mrs. Hannigan."

172
00:07:40,794 --> 00:07:42,379
Wrong again.

173
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:46,341
Apparently, you can change it
to anything you want,

174
00:07:46,383 --> 00:07:48,385
so I thought, all right,
here's an opportunity

175
00:07:48,427 --> 00:07:49,803
to be creative...

176
00:07:49,844 --> 00:07:54,141
so, meet...
Princess Consuela Bananahammock.

177
00:07:59,938 --> 00:08:02,316
That's what we were
going to name the baby.

178
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:05,819
Phoebe...

179
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:09,197
Uh, Princess Consuela.

180
00:08:09,239 --> 00:08:11,741
You seriously changed
your name to that?
Uh-huh.

181
00:08:11,783 --> 00:08:14,661
Okay, so from now on,
we have to call you
Princess Consuela?

182
00:08:14,702 --> 00:08:18,039
Um, no, I-I'm going to have
my friends call me Valerie.

183
00:08:22,002 --> 00:08:23,503
Hey, how'd the
interview go?

184
00:08:23,544 --> 00:08:25,339
Oh... not good.

185
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:27,674
You know, I always feel that way
after an interview.

186
00:08:27,715 --> 00:08:29,343
I'll bet it went better
than you think.

187
00:08:29,384 --> 00:08:31,011
Well, I didn't get

188
00:08:31,052 --> 00:08:34,806
the job at Gucci, and I got
fired from Ralph Lauren.

189
00:08:34,848 --> 00:08:37,225
That is a bad interview.

190
00:08:37,267 --> 00:08:39,353
What are you...? Well, what
are you talking about?

191
00:08:39,394 --> 00:08:41,062
How'd this happen?
Well, my boss

192
00:08:41,104 --> 00:08:44,191
was at the same restaurant
where I was having my interview,

193
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:46,318
and he heard everything,
so later,

194
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,028
he calls me into his
office and he tells me

195
00:08:48,069 --> 00:08:49,529
that he's going
to have to let me go

196
00:08:49,570 --> 00:08:51,198
because I'm not a team player,

197
00:08:51,239 --> 00:08:52,366
and I say, "Wait a minute.

198
00:08:52,407 --> 00:08:53,741
No, yes, I am,"

199
00:08:53,783 --> 00:08:56,203
and then I had to sit there
for 45 minutes

200
00:08:56,244 --> 00:09:01,749
while he proved that that,
in fact... was true.

201
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:03,918
Oh, God, I'm so sorry.

202
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:04,878
( sighs )

203
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:06,713
Hey.

204
00:09:06,754 --> 00:09:09,883
What? Ooh, wh-what's this?

205
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:12,552
Why, it's... it's a bottle
of champagne.

206
00:09:12,593 --> 00:09:14,262
Well, why is this here?

207
00:09:14,304 --> 00:09:15,263
Ross...

208
00:09:15,305 --> 00:09:16,555
I guess it's here because...

209
00:09:16,597 --> 00:09:17,974
I got tenure!

210
00:09:18,016 --> 00:09:20,060
Wow.
Congratulations.

211
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:23,522
This is the single greatest day
of my professional career.

212
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:24,772
Gunther, six glasses!

213
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:25,773
Six?

214
00:09:25,815 --> 00:09:27,234
You-you want me to join you?

215
00:09:27,275 --> 00:09:29,528
Oh, I thought Joey was here.
Five is good.

216
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:35,742
Wow, I'm going to have a loogie
in my coffee tomorrow.

217
00:09:37,452 --> 00:09:40,038
Ooh, Israeli champagne...

218
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:42,249
and it's vanilla.

219
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:45,793
I got tenure.
I didn't win the lottery.

220
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:48,755
Hey, Rach, so, uh,
how did your thing go?

221
00:09:48,796 --> 00:09:50,882
Oh, it went good, yeah,
but I'm not going to hear

222
00:09:50,924 --> 00:09:52,926
about that for a couple
of days.

223
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:55,220
Oh, you know what?
You're going to get it.
I-I-I-I can feel it.

224
00:09:55,262 --> 00:09:57,097
Can you?

225
00:09:57,138 --> 00:09:59,807
Well, everybody,
here's to Ross.

226
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:05,397
And-and to years of hard
work finally paying off.

227
00:10:05,439 --> 00:10:08,316
And to knowing that your career
doesn't mean everything.

228
00:10:08,358 --> 00:10:10,693
But also knowing it means

229
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:13,029
a lot.

230
00:10:13,071 --> 00:10:14,489
But more importantly,

231
00:10:14,531 --> 00:10:15,949
to full,
well-rounded lives.

232
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:17,867
That center around work.

233
00:10:17,909 --> 00:10:20,579
To Ross!
To Ross!

234
00:10:24,207 --> 00:10:26,042
You know what the best
part about this is?

235
00:10:26,084 --> 00:10:27,586
I can never be fired.

236
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:29,170
Oh, God...
No, seriously.

237
00:10:29,212 --> 00:10:32,048
I have job
security for life.

238
00:10:32,090 --> 00:10:34,217
You know, I mean, I
never have to worry.

239
00:10:34,259 --> 00:10:35,552
Oh, oh, look at you.

240
00:10:35,594 --> 00:10:37,762
Look how happy
you are for me.

241
00:10:40,432 --> 00:10:42,058
( sniffles ):
No, it's not that.

242
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:43,893
I got fired today...

243
00:10:43,935 --> 00:10:46,104
and I didn't get
the other job.

244
00:10:48,273 --> 00:10:49,608
Oh, my God.

245
00:10:49,649 --> 00:10:50,900
Rach, I'm so sorry.

246
00:10:50,942 --> 00:10:52,735
Oh...

247
00:10:52,777 --> 00:10:54,695
Great. I feel
like an idiot.

248
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:57,907
No, it's okay.
You didn't know.
Oh...

249
00:10:57,949 --> 00:11:00,076
A little heads-up
would've been nice.

250
00:11:09,669 --> 00:11:11,546
Thank you for letting
us see the house again.

251
00:11:11,588 --> 00:11:13,840
And thank you for explaining
to us what escrow means.

252
