I was staring at her baby.

523
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:16,358
We're about to be parents.

524
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:19,195
Oh. Sorry.

525
00:21:28,871 --> 00:21:31,040
Hi, you guys.

526
00:21:31,082 --> 00:21:32,208
Hi. So, uh...
Hi.

527
00:21:32,250 --> 00:21:33,459
how was dinner?

528
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:34,627
Oh, it was great.

529
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:35,795
Mark is so sweet.

530
00:21:35,836 --> 00:21:36,796
Oh, yeah?

531
00:21:36,837 --> 00:21:38,256
Yeah. I wonder why.

532
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:39,966
What could that smarmy
letch possibly want?

533
00:21:40,007 --> 00:21:41,134
Oh, Ross.

534
00:21:41,175 --> 00:21:42,301
Come on.

535
00:21:42,342 --> 00:21:43,803
He is happily married.

536
00:21:43,844 --> 00:21:45,387
His wife just had twins.

537
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:47,640
Should we send something?

538
00:21:48,682 --> 00:21:50,768
How did the
job stuff go?

539
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:53,271
He offered me one.

540
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:55,439
That's great.
Oh, my God!

541
00:21:55,481 --> 00:21:56,816
Congratulations.

542
00:21:56,857 --> 00:21:58,734
I know. It's amazing.

543
00:21:58,776 --> 00:22:00,236
It's amazing.

544
00:22:00,278 --> 00:22:02,529
It's so much better
than what I had at Ralph Lauren.

545
00:22:02,571 --> 00:22:04,865
The money is great.

546
00:22:04,907 --> 00:22:06,993
Can we... Can we just
stop for a second?

547
00:22:07,034 --> 00:22:10,037
Who said something better
would come along, huh?

548
00:22:10,079 --> 00:22:11,538
You didn't
believe me.

549
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:12,999
I told you everything
was going to work out.

550
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:14,083
( gasps )

551
00:22:14,125 --> 00:22:15,584
You know what?

552
00:22:15,626 --> 00:22:16,961
This calls for a bottle
of Israel's finest!

553
00:22:20,881 --> 00:22:23,634
The job is in Paris.

554
00:22:31,017 --> 00:22:34,687
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

555
00:22:36,022 --> 00:22:38,691
I mean, the soap opera's
a great gig,

556
00:22:38,732 --> 00:22:41,277
but am I missing opportunities?

557
00:22:41,319 --> 00:22:43,904
You know, I've always thought
of myself as a serious actor.

558
00:22:43,946 --> 00:22:47,033
I mean, should I be trying
to do more independent movies?

559
00:22:47,074 --> 00:22:49,160
I don't know.

560
00:22:50,244 --> 00:22:51,537
But you know what?

561
00:22:51,578 --> 00:22:53,289
I'm going to put you
on with my bear.

562
00:22:53,331 --> 00:22:55,916
Hold on.

563
00:22:55,958 --> 00:22:58,460
Hey, bear,
I need some career advice.

